            "review_title": "Review at Texas Chicken",
            "review_text": "DirtyPierreOnTour\nHo Chi Minh City, Vietnam12578 contributions\n0\n1st off. I'm not a fan of fast food.\nJul 2018 • Solo\nBut after putting their name in Google I learnt they were an American chain of fried chicken outlets under the name of Churches in Texas. When they went global with their franchise they changed it to Texas Fried Chicken. I was curious to see how in compared to the well known KFC. I went into their outlet on Phan Xich Long which is street almost dedicated to restaurants some of which are foreign chains although most are Korean BBQ.\nFirst I was impressed with the cleanliness and smiling friendly staff. Perusing the menu I was impressed the had healthy options of flat bread wraps. I chose the spicy Mexican wrap with a side of coleslaw and a bottomless cup of serve yourself soft drink. The wrap had both crunchy texture and delicious spicy flavour. Coleslaw was moist with plenty of tasty dressing in the cup. I refilled my drink only once as two cups of soft drink is plenty for me.\nOverall a pleasant experience that I have repeated at least once a month ever since the last visit being two nights ago.\nI don't like their French fries but then I prefer chips which are thicker and unevenly cut. I felt their mashed potato was too salty for my liking so haven't reordered that since. So one chicken wrap and a side of coleslaw with bottomless drink for 79,000vnd is good value lunch meal in my book. It beats anything KFC has to offer in Vietnam in my opinion.\nRead more\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten July 10, 2018",
            "rating": 5.0,
